+// (round 11) tri_slot_sum (M_t / vector segments) + tri_param_finish in ONE launch.  At L128 d_pair 128 the two kernels are 4.9 + 3.5
+// us of almost no work: the slot sum is NOT bound by its bytes (B200 2026-11-18: the same 4.9-5.1 us with 19 MB or, cluster-summed,
+// 2.4 MB of M_t slots), so the second launch is the cost.  Block b < 512 = the M_t row (t, c) = b: its 32 float4 columns summed over
+// the slots by 16 slot lanes (lane g: slots g, g + 16, ..; the lane sums added in lane order -- tri_slot_sum's order: the same M bits),
+// cs_t the same way, then dW_t[o][c] = gamma_c M + beta_c cs_t[o] for the row's 128 o and the row's shares of dgamma / dbeta
+// (sum_o W_t[o][c] M, sum_o W_t[o][c] cs_t[o], a fixed shuffle order) into WS; blocks 512..515 sum B_h, block 516 cdb.  The last block
+// to arrive (a self-resetting ticket) adds the four tensors' shares a channel in t order and writes dgamma | dbeta | dWb.
+template <typename OutT>
+__global__ void __launch_bounds__(512) tri_slot_finish(const float* __restrict__ MTS, const float* __restrict__ VECS, const int nsp,
